_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","login":"StarryWorm","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm"},"body":"The test file does not cover the case whereby the class extends one of its const members as written out in the proposal, i.e.\n```gdscript\nextends Const\n\nconst Const = preload(\"some_script.gd\")\n```\nMaybe one of the tests cases covers it indirectly, but I would prefer if we had an explicit test case, which would likely look like a \n```gdscript\n# inner_const_base.gd\nclass_name InnerConstBase extends _InnerBase\n\nconst _InnerBase = preload(\"inner_base.gd\")\n```","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121171#pullrequestreview-4755806976","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121171","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-07-22T15:05:12Z"},{"id":4755848481,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG3h9IQ","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"7f9b7257982b1a93536ba66bf67635c846a74c27","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?u=8069d9b7bc6ab503ce83dfcfa53fd021672aeccf&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","login":"Mickeon","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon"},"body":"After properly understanding the issue myself, I do approve of this. With the hierarchical approach that GDScript encourages, it really doesn't make sense. Unfortunately cannot speak on the code itself.\n_Intentionally_ keeping this feature is bound to not work, either.\nBut my prior comment still stands. Just in case, worth mentioning in migration guide and/or blog post.",